---Send heartbeat
---
---Sends one legacy order heartbeat for the authenticated API key.
---The first accepted send enables timeout cancellation for all open orders
---owned by that API key, across markets and processes. Keep sending accepted
---heartbeats every 5 seconds. No scheduler or disarm operation is provided;
---stopping sends or closing a client leaves the deadline active.
---It shares the key's registration with POST /v1/heartbeats and resets the
---expected modern heartbeat ID to an empty string.
---After 10 seconds without an accepted send, a five-second scan removes the
---registration and queues a best-effort cancel-all attempt. Cancellation
---timing and success are not guaranteed. Later accepted sends register again.
---A lost response may follow an accepted send. WebSocket keepalive does not
---refresh this deadline. Stop placing orders and explicitly cancel/verify
---orders you intend to remove before shutdown.
---
---`POST /heartbeats`
---@param input? polymarket.clob.SendHeartbeatRequest
---@return polymarket.clob.HeartbeatResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:send_heartbeat(input) end

---Send heartbeat (v1)
---
---Sends one order heartbeat with a rotating ID for the authenticated API key.
---The first accepted send enables timeout cancellation for all open orders
---owned by that API key, across markets and processes. Keep sending accepted
---heartbeats every 5 seconds. No scheduler or disarm operation is provided;
---stopping sends or closing a client leaves the deadline active.
---
---Start with an empty heartbeat_id and retain each new ID returned by a
---successful response. Serialize sends per key. A mismatch returns HTTP 400
---with error_msg "Invalid Heartbeat ID" and the currently expected
---heartbeat_id, which may be empty after a legacy send. Retry explicitly with
---that ID. Rejected requests do not refresh the deadline. A lost response may
---follow an accepted send, so failure does not prove registration is inactive.
---
---After 10 seconds without an accepted send, a five-second scan removes the
---registration and queues a best-effort cancel-all attempt. Cancellation
---timing and success are not guaranteed. Later accepted sends register again.
---WebSocket keepalive does not refresh this deadline. Stop placing orders and
---explicitly cancel/verify orders you intend to remove before shutdown.
---
---`POST /v1/heartbeats`
---@param input polymarket.clob.SendHeartbeatV1Request
---@return polymarket.clob.HeartbeatV1Response? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:send_heartbeat_v1(input) end

